# AI policy

Full text: `doc/AI_POLICY.md` (adapted from Bitcoin Core). High bar for all contributions.

## Required behavior

- Human author in the loop: choose the work, understand the change, own the contribution.
- Do not open or drive pull requests autonomously.
- Do not set an agent as git author or co-author.
- Do not draft GitHub issue/PR comments or review replies meant to be posted as-is; humans write those in their own words.
- Only propose changes the human could have written and can explain (language, surrounding code, effects).

## Disclosure

If AI interaction context is useful in a comment, it must be disclosed and paired with human commentary on relevance and implications.

## Agent practice

Prefer small, reviewable diffs. Help explore and draft; leave PR bodies, review answers, and commit authorship to the human. Violations can get PRs closed without notice.
